  "subtitle": "spiced almond pastry rounds sandwiched with raspberry jam",
  "excerpt": "Linzer cookies are small versions of the Austrian Linzer torte: a cinnamon-spiced almond pastry cut into rounds, sandwiched with raspberry jam, and dusted with icing sugar through a cut-out window in the top piece that reveals the jam beneath. The pastry is short, crumbly, and fragrant with almond and cinnamon. A little care is needed when rolling: the ground almond content makes the dough more delicate than a plain flour biscuit and the cut-out tops must be lifted cleanly.",
