  "sourceNotes": "Linzer cookies are a miniaturised form of the Linzer torte, an Austrian pastry considered one of the world's oldest known cakes (documented from 1653). The cookie format (Linzer Augen, Linzer eyes) became popularised in the late 19th and early 20th centuries in the Austro-Hungarian Empire and was brought to North America by Austrian and German immigrants. The recipe follows the classic Linzer pastry formulation as documented in Austrian baking references including Katharina Prato's Süddeutsche Küche (1858 onward) and later sources.",
