  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Linzer pastry is made like a shortcrust: cold butter rubbed into the flour and almond mixture, bound with egg yolks. The ground almonds make it more crumbly than plain shortbread, so the dough needs to be cold when rolled and the cut-out tops must be transferred on a palette knife. Refrigerate the cut rounds again before baking if they have softened. A small star or round cutter for the window gives the cleanest result."
          }
        ]
      },
