      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Combine {{plain-flour}}, {{ground-almonds}}, {{caster-sugar}}, {{cinnamon-ground}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} in a large bowl. Rub in {{unsalted-butter}} until the mixture looks like damp sand with a few pea-sized lumps. Add {{egg-yolks}} and {{vanilla-extract}} and press together to form a dough. If it feels dry, add 1 teaspoon of cold water. Divide in two, flatten each half into a disc, wrap, and refrigerate for 1 hour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Roll and cut"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 170°C (conventional). Line two baking trays. Roll one disc on a lightly floured surface to 4 mm thickness. Cut into 6 cm rounds; these are the solid bases. Roll the second disc and cut into 6 cm rounds; then, using a small cutter (about 2 cm), cut a window from the centre of each of these top rounds. Transfer all rounds to the lined trays on a palette knife. Refrigerate for 15 minutes if they have softened. Bake for 12 to 14 minutes until pale golden at the edges. Cool completely on a wire rack."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assemble"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dust the top rounds (the ones with the window cut-out) generously with {{icing-sugar}}. Spread a generous teaspoon of {{raspberry-jam}} onto the centre of each solid base round, spreading almost to the edges. Lay a dusted top round over each base and press gently to sandwich. Do not fill them more than 1 hour before serving; the jam softens the pastry if left too long."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
